 - 2026-06-15: PHASE A2 (HEADLINE; cross-check the surprising win) -- MULTI-SEED + INDEPENDENT replication of the +44pp ARC oracle-distinct win. exp4245 reported delta +0.4423 on a SINGLE seed (4245), n=52. A surprising result is not headline-eligible until replicated (n>1 seeds, same direction; CLAUDE.md). RE-RUN the decisive beats-vote gate across >=5 SEEDS (independent fold reshuffles of the train/held-out split over the grown pool), report per-seed delta + the MEAN delta + a cross-seed CI (and flag any seed where the win flips sign). SEPARATELY, an INDEPENDENT clean-room re-score: reload the persisted A1/.393 pool artifact and recompute set_encoder@1, vote@1, oracle@K via a SECOND code path (not the .393 script) to confirm the numbers reproduce off the artifact (mirrors the G2 FoVer independent-reproducer pattern). Emit oracle_distinct_win_replicates BARE bool := (mean cross-seed delta>0 AND cross-seed CI excl 0 AND the independent re-score lands within the .393 CI). verifier_is_oracle=false. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: arc_oracle_distinct_win_replicates_multiseed; results/experiment_4257_arc_oracle_distinct_multiseed_replication.json
