 - 2026-06-15: PHASE A4 (EXTEND the win; gated_on A1 win_survives_provenance_blind AND A2 oracle_distinct_win_replicates) -- selection->SYNTHESIS: break the oracle@K ceiling. The .393 win is SELECTION (pick the best cached candidate), capped at oracle@K=0.827 -- 17% of held-out tasks have NO correct candidate, so selection can NEVER solve them. Compute-as-Teacher (2509.14234) + Generative-Aggregation (2503.04104): SYNTHESIS can construct an answer that EXCEEDS the best rollout. Build an AggLM-style review-reconcile-SYNTHESIZE step: DeepSets-weighted per-CELL reconciliation over the top-ranked candidate family (weight each candidate's per-cell vote by the learned set-encoder score) -> a synthesized grid that MAY differ from every candidate; validate by EXACT ARC grid match. Report synthesis@1 vs vote@1 vs selector-only@1 (the .393 set-encoder) vs a no-synthesis baseline vs oracle@K, task-level bootstrap CI95. Headline target: synthesis@1 > oracle@K on the held-out split (recovering tasks where NO candidate was correct). verifier_is_oracle=false. Fabrication guard: EXACT grid-match gate + the explicit no-synthesis control (per the .393 SOTA-ingestion warning). (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: arc_synthesis_underperforms_selection; results/experiment_4259_arc_agglm_grid_synthesis.json
